# Line endings are LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Without this file, git relied on core.autocrlf, which on Windows rewrote 377
# tracked text files to CRLF on checkout. The contract suite asserts exact
# multi-line source strings — for example
# `signedAdminCommandArguments(\n      'product_media_upload'` — so a CRLF
# working tree silently fails security contracts even though the code is intact.
# Checkout must be byte-identical to what the tests expect.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
